## SQ-CDJ-11 | old world: pre-nest jars load and their blocks are placed
@group A (Boot 0)
@commands Boot with the five displaced jars added; `grep -n "is loaded from\|members:" logs/latest.log`; place: Display plate, plated hamburger (`displaydelight:` plated id), `beef_stew`, a cake slice on a small plate, 3 cookies on a plate (for SQ-DDP-07); Pickling Jar with garlic + honey bottle mid-batch; Cheese Wheel at `bites=0`; Veggies and Vintage crops on farmland; a Fungi colony; a Copper Pot on a lit campfire holding ingredients; a Sticky Basket with items. Note the coordinates in the run notes; `/save-all`; stop
@pass five ERROR lines `[creativedelight] member <id> is loaded from backported...jar ..., not from the Creative Delight jar` (proves the old code ran); `Done (`; every block placed
@fails No ERROR line: the displaced jar was not picked up (check `OUT/srv/mods/`); crash: a displaced jar needs a CD class that moved (record, then build the old world without that member)
